Emit a hull shader's patch-constant function returning void on the GLSL target.

invokePatchConstantFuncInHullShader (source/slang/slang-ir-glsl-legalize.cpp) legalizes the
patch-constant function's result as it does an entry point's: legalizeEntryPointReturnValueForGLSL
writes the returned struct to gl_TessLevelOuter, gl_TessLevelInner and the patch outputs, and
replaces each return with one that has no value. It then calls fixUpFuncType(constantFunc), which
keeps the function's declared result type, while the entry point beside it gets
fixUpFuncType(entryPoint, builder.getVoidType()). The GLSL target therefore emits
`TePatch_0 teConstants_0(...) { ... return; }`, and glslang refuses it: "'return' : non-void
function must return a value".

This gives the patch-constant function a void result type, as the entry point has. A regression
test is added as tools/slang-unit-test/unit-test-glsl-patch-constant-function-void.cpp.

Measured on v2026.21: glslangValidator -V --target-env vulkan1.2 -S tesc refused the hull shader's
GLSL (the SPIR-V target's module passed spirv-val).
diff --git a/source/slang/slang-ir-glsl-legalize.cpp b/source/slang/slang-ir-glsl-legalize.cpp
index f34e007df..d4a5713aa 100644
--- a/source/slang/slang-ir-glsl-legalize.cpp
+++ b/source/slang/slang-ir-glsl-legalize.cpp
@@ -1469,7 +1469,11 @@ void invokePatchConstantFuncInHullShader(
 
     addPatchDecorationToNonSystemValueLeaves(&builder, patchConstantFuncOutputVal);
 
-    fixUpFuncType(constantFunc);
+    // The legalization above writes the result to the patch-constant outputs and turns every
+    // `return` into one without a value, as for the entry point itself, so the function no longer
+    // returns its struct.
+    //
+    fixUpFuncType(constantFunc, builder.getVoidType());
 }
 
 static bool targetBuiltinRequiresLegalization(IRTargetBuiltinVarName builtinVarName)
